### Fix 2 — Keep per-place cards, drop widget chips, render cards near top

User wants the rich per-place cards (address + "Open in Maps" button) — they convey more than the widget's chip list. The chips are the redundancy to remove.

**2a. Drop the chip list in the widget config.** File: `static/js/family_assistant_shared.js:135-143`. Remove the `PlaceContextualListConfigElement` append so the widget renders the map only (markers stay, chips gone):
```js
// delete the if-block adding <gmp-place-contextual-list-config>
```
Cards below the map already enumerate the places with full detail.

**2b. Move cards above the map widget.** File: `static/js/family_agent.js:411-417` and mirror in `static/js/clancy_assistant.js`. Reorder so action_suggestions render before the widget:
```js
renderRunError(message, cards);
(message.action_suggestions || []).forEach((s) => cards.appendChild(renderActionSuggestion(s)));
renderGoogleMapsGroundingWidget(message.context_json || {}, cards, { apiKey: googleMapsClientApiKey });
(message.proposals || []).forEach(...);
(message.memory_suggestions || []).forEach(...);
```
Now the visual flow: assistant text → place cards → map for context → other proposals.

No backend prompt change needed. Server contract unchanged.

